# Project: TaskFlow API

A REST API for task management built with Express.js and TypeScript.
Stack: Node.js 20, Express 4, PostgreSQL 16, Prisma ORM, Zod validation.
Deployed on Railway. CI runs on GitHub Actions.

## Conventions
- All files use TypeScript strict mode
- Functions use explicit return types (no inferred returns)
- Error handling uses custom AppError class in src/lib/errors.ts
- Database queries go through Prisma, never raw SQL
- API responses follow the shape in src/lib/response.ts
- Tests use Vitest with the patterns in tests/helpers/

## Structure
- src/routes/ //API route handlers (one file per resource)
- src/services/ //Business logic (called by routes, calls Prisma)
- src/lib/ //Shared utilities and types
- src/middleware/ //Express middleware
- tests/ //Mirror of src/ structure with .test.ts suffix
- prisma/ //Schema and migrations (do NOT edit migrations manually)

## Rules
- Never run git push without explicit user approval
- Never delete files in src/ without reading them first
- Never modify .env or .env.local files
- Always run `npm test` after modifying any file in src/
- When creating new routes, always add corresponding tests
- If a test fails, fix the code, don't fix the test to pass

## Workflow
- Show me the plan before making changes to more than 3 files
- Commit messages follow conventional commits (feat:, fix:, refactor:)
- When I ask for a code review, check for: type safety, error handling,
  test coverage, and SQL injection vectors
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones

